What I Learned About Printing Hello, World! in C

Today, I learned how to write my first C program in VS Code.

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    return 0;
}

What I Learned
#include <stdio.h> is used to include the standard input/output library.
int main() is the main function where the program starts running.
printf() is used to print text on the screen.
Text must be written inside double quotation marks (" ").
The semicolon (;) is used to end a statement in C.
\n moves the cursor to a new line.
return 0; indicates that the program finished successfully.

Output

Hello, World!

Conclusion

I learned how to write, save, and run a simple C program in VS Code. This is my first step toward learning C programming.